  "text": "<p>XXXIX. — Cold becomes warm, and warm, cold; wet becomes dry, and dry, wet.</p><p><br>XL. —  It disperses and gathers, it comes and goes.</p><p><br>XLI. — Into the same river you could not step twice, for other and still other waters are flowing.</p><p><br>XLII. — To those entering the same river, other and still other waters flow.</p>",
